%S A401451 1,3,119,13761,3178785,1226341035,711310157271,578808021857625,
%T A401451 629094292867153665,880420061542046903955,1542142783860061524297975,
%U A401451 3305066423033878298552132145,8507914454392557998456492959905,25904184766695256133740113683890875,92081681670993767861604318182744220375,377918381088551807930976158989611272990025
%N A401451 Number of Young tableaux with walls of period n whose basic blocks are Z2, where Z2 is a special class of Young diagram with walls of shape 2 X 2.
%C A401451 Z2 is given explicitly in Banderier and Wallner.
%C A401451 A recurrence formula was derived by Liu, Liu, and Xin.
%H A401451 Cyril Banderier and Michael Wallner, <a href="https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~slc/wpapers/FPSAC2021/47.html">Young tableaux with periodic walls: counting with the density method</a>, Séminaire Lotharingien de Combinatoire 85B (2021), Article #47.
%H A401451 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a401/A401451.java">Java program</a> (github)
%H A401451 Feihu Liu, Jiahang Liu, and Guoce Xin, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.35067">Two families of Young tableaux with periodic walls: Counting formulas and differential transcendence</a>, arXiv:2610.35067 [math.CO], (2026).
%F A401451 a(n+1) = (4n)! * Integral_{0 < t_1 < t_2 < ... < t_{2n} < 1} Product_{k=1..n} (1 - t_{2k}^2)/2 dt_1 ... dt_{2n}, where t_1, ..., t_{2n} are the entries of the top row.
%K A401451 nonn,new
%O A401451 1,2
%A A401451 _Feihu Liu_, Oct 25 2026
